  "description":"Reciprocal construction for given skew lines a/b: auxiliary a1 through M is parallel to given b; auxiliary b1 through N is parallel to given a. Alpha/beta are separately closed rounded source plane-patch contours, not measured ellipses. Original upper-plane glyph remains UNKNOWN; displayed beta is explicitly TEXT-DERIVED MODERN RELABELLING from the approved solution, NOT recovery of source glyph. All four source line roles and M/N dark junctions retained without added interplane connectors or solved dimensions. Internal transparent regions serve only containment assertions.",
  "source":{
    "image":{"path":"ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/9-10g/figures/fig-36.png","sha256":"ffe0ea1da293252f0a624531370a67e36078ff2218d4b4eef34dd202bf5c3ed7"},
    "authoritativeText":[
      {"lesson":"geo910-c1-s1-n11","text":"§11. 关于平行平面的定理"},
      {"lesson":"geo910-c1-s1-n11","text":"解。\n过直线 $a$ 上的任意点 $M$，作直线 $a_1$ 与直线 $b$ 平行（图 36），再过 $a$ 和 $a_1$ 作平面 $\\alpha$。\n用类似的方法作平面 $\\beta$。\n\n根据平面平行的判定定理，平面 $\\alpha$ 和 $\\beta$ 平行。"},
      {"lesson":"geo910-c1-s1-n11","text":"推论。\n如果两个已知平面都与另一个平面平行，那么这两个已知平面平行。"},
      {"lesson":"geo910-c1-s1-n11","text":"请自行证明，可以尝试用反证法（图 35）。"},
      {"lesson":"geo910-c1-s1-n11","text":"图　35"},
      {"lesson":"geo910-c1-s1-n11","text":"图　36"},
      {"lesson":"geo910-c1-s1-n11","text":"问题。\n分别过两条异面直线作平面，使这两个平面平行。"}
    ],
    "inventory":[
